	(footprint "meenie:TestPad_0.6mm_PTH"
		(layer "B.Cu")
		(uuid "7969a7ff-90b9-4e68-984f-f2f4416d94db")
		(at 105.528 91.114999)
		(descr "0.80 mm round plated through hole breakout on a 0.50 mm finished hole, 0.15 mm annular ring at JLCPCB's minimum. 0.50 mm is the smallest plated hole JLCPCB will not flood with mask or tin and finishes at 0.42 mm worst case against their plus 0.13 minus 0.08 tolerance, which still admits 30 AWG solid at 0.254 mm. The ring is the minimum rather than the recommended 0.20 because the 1.68 mm north band between U1's courtyard and the panel tab pullback holds two staggered rows of 0.80 mm pads and only one row of 0.90 mm. Land, via seat and layer transition in one object. Declared as a pad rather than a via so it keeps a mask opening and is excluded from epoxy via fill.")
